WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.970
This year, in the midst of
many challenges, we have been so grateful

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:08.408
for you, our community. You've continued
to show up in so many different ways,

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.478
even as the ways we work with
and live have changed.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.547
You've used data to answer questions
important to you,

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:19.419
written insightful code, helped people learn,
and continued to share everything you do

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.956
with your communities,
coworkers, neighbors, family and friends.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:27.727
Thank you for your kindness,
your curiosity, and bringing all of you

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:32.599
to the ways that you work with and share
about data. From RStudio Open Source,

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.034
thank you.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:40.940
Thank you.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.975
Thank you.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:42.943
[GERMAN: Thank you very much.]

00:00:42.943 --> 00:00:44.244
[FRENCH: Thank you.]

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:48.181
Thank you. 

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.851
[FRENCH: Thank you.]

00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:53.486
A big thank you to the entire open
source community. [TELUGU: Thank you.] 

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.221
Thank you.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.690
[TURKISH: Thank you.]

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:57.558
Thank you.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.225
Hey, you're using the things we made, and

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.361
I really appreciate that. Thank you.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.529
[FRENCH: Thank you.]

00:01:02.563 --> 00:01:04.464
Thank you.

00:01:04.498 --> 00:01:07.034
[MARA, VOICEOVER: You wanna say thank you?]

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.835
Thank you. 
[MANDARIN: Thank you.] 

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.835
[CANTONESE: Thank you.] 
[JAPANESE: Thank you.]

00:01:10.835 --> 00:01:12.406
Thank you.

00:01:12.406 --> 00:01:13.807
Thank you.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.209
Thank you
for all the ways you contribute and share.

